      "side": 1,
      "message": "That scenario is possible, but the branch starting at line 419 handles it.\n\nThere is still a very small bug here since `dmabuf_count` is a `size_t`, and the read could possibly be non-atomic. However it\u0027s extremely unlikely any process refers to `2^32 + 1` different buffers... that\u0027d take at least 128G of kernel memory to reach.",
